                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>With population aging, strengthening medical services for older adults is essential to safeguard their health. Physicians should accurately understand the characteristics of age-related declines in organ function and provide precise diagnosis and treatment tailored to older patients’ physical and psychological needs. Meanwhile, efforts should be made to enhance doctor–patient communication skills, patiently address patients’ questions, relieve their anxiety, and promote a harmonious doctor–patient relationship. Such measures can help improve the health support system for older adults and provide strong protection for their well-being.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
